[2026-10-20T23:07:06.813Z] [INFO]       "output": "Hive Mind 2026-10-20 (0.354.1): Hello World via /claude, /codex and /agent all failed (branch 'so', web_run {} ×210, build outputs left, invalid gh flags, scalac missing, exit code misread, workflow never planned): everything the next release must fix\n\n## Summary\n\nOn 2026-10-20 Hive Mind 2.39.2 ran the three Hello World issues with Formal AI **0.354.1** as the model, one per client. **None succeeded:**\n\n| Client | Issue / PR | Execution | Result | What Formal AI produced in this run |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Claude Code (`--tool claude`) | [Kotlin #1](https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb330-fa49-7c9d-a664-b7ea33bb698a/issues/1) / [PR #2](https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb330-fa49-7c9d-a664-b7ea33bb698a/pull/2) | `2719fb28` | **failed, exit 1** after 7 min 28 s | Session 1: correct `Main.kt`, verify script, compiled, ran, committed and pushed `139e03c`. Left `Main.jar` untracked. Session 2 (restart for `Main.jar`): an invalid `gh` command, then stopped |\n| Codex (`--tool codex`) | [Rust #1](https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/issues/1) / [PR #2](https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/pull/2) | `b8b78e59` | **stopped by the operator, exit 137**, after 14 h 8 min | `main.rs` + verify script, compiled and ran, committed. **Pushed to branch `so`** (fails), then **210** `web_run` calls with `{}` until the sidecar was stopped. No workflow |\n| Agent CLI (`--tool agent`) | [Scala #1](https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb330-00e1-73b9-955e-f357a1600d5b/issues/1) / [PR #2](https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb330-00e1-73b9-955e-f357a1600d5b/pull/2) | `2e56df93` | **failed, exit 1** after 2 h 39 min | Nothing new: 7 attempts, each repeated the same reads and writes and stopped at `scalac: not found` |\n\nGoal of this issue: everything Formal AI must change so that the **next release completes all three runs**. Each item below has the evidence from these logs, the related issue if one exists, and a regression test built from this exact input. Parts outside Formal AI are listed at the end and tracked in their own repositories.\n\nThis continues #1162 (the same three tasks on 2026-09-27 with 0.352.1) and #1328 (the Codex loop of this run, observed live).\n\n## What went wrong, per task\n\n### 1. Claude Code, Kotlin (`2719fb28`, 14:14 → 14:21 UTC)\n\n1. Session 1 (`858bf47a`, 7 turns) did the work correctly:\n   - `gh issue view` (title and body);\n   - wrote `Main.kt` and `tests/verify-output.sh`;\n   - ran `kotlinc Main.kt -include-runtime -d Main.jar`, then the verify script (`Hello, World!`);\n   - `git add … && git commit … && git push -q origin 'issue-1-604f2202fd18'` → `139e03c`, pushed.\n\n   It ended `subtype=success` with \"Created and verified `Main.kt` through the agentic CLI harness.\"\n2. **`Main.jar` was left untracked** in the working tree: Formal AI's own build command writes it into the repository root. Hive Mind restarts the session for every uncommitted file (#1157 has the same symptom from 2026-09-27).\n3. Session 2 (`539e9b34`, 2 turns) got Hive Mind's restart prompt, which lists `?? Main.jar` and asks to commit, ignore or delete each file. Formal AI did none of that. Its only step was:\n   ```\n   gh pr view 'https://github.com/…/pull/2' --comments --json comments,reviews\n   → Exit code 1: specify only one of --comments or --json\n   ```\n   It then ended with \"Prepared-work continuation stopped at `gh pr view …`\". The usage error names the fix (`--json comments,reviews` alone), but Formal AI neither retried it nor moved on to the actual request (`Main.jar`).\n4. Hive Mind then stopped with \"no progress between sessions\" (same HEAD `139e03c`, `Main.jar` still there), exit 1.\n\nThe PR content is close to complete: `Main.kt`, the verify script and `.github/workflows/run.yml` (from the 2026-09-27 run) are there, and CI passes. What failed the run is the build output and the second session.\n\n### 2. Codex, Rust (`b8b78e59`, 08:27 → 22:36 UTC)\n\nDetails and the live observation are in #1328. Final numbers:\n\n1. 08:41:50: `rustc main.rs -o main`, the verify script passed, and `git commit` succeeded. **`git push -q origin 'so'`** then failed with `error: src refspec so does not match any`. The branch name came from the system prompt's guideline sentence \"commit each atomic step … to the pull request **branch so** interrupted work remains preserved\". The real branch `issue-1-09b0c76bd0e4` appears 11 times in the same Codex session (`turn_context.git.branch`, the prompt).\n2. 08:43:55 → 16:35:10: **210** `codex_apps search_service.web_run` calls, all with `arguments: {}`, all rejected (`InvalidActionArgumentsError … missing_required_argument`). Before every call the text was the same: \"Let me search the web for rust src refspec so does not match any.\" There was no repeat stop. Each answer used 57–140 s of a full core, and the request body grew by 864 B per call.\n3. After the sidecar was stopped (16:35:50), Codex waited \"for network\" until the operator stopped the task at 22:36. Hive Mind then auto-committed and pushed the untracked **`main` binary (4.5 MB)** that Formal AI's `rustc main.rs -o main` had left in the repository root (`693630a`). The same build-output problem as `Main.jar`.\n4. **Requirement 6 (a GitHub Actions workflow) was never planned**: the PR has no workflow and no CI.\n\n### 3. Agent CLI, Scala (`2e56df93`, 14:28 → 17:07 UTC)\n\n1. Every attempt repeated the same steps: `gh issue view` ×2, write `Main.scala`, write `tests/verify-output.sh`, `scalac Main.scala` → `/bin/sh: 1: scalac: not found` (exit 127), then stop. There were 7 attempts: the first plus 6 Hive Mind retries of the same session; the last one failed at once on the stopped sidecar. `scalac` ran 8 times. **No commit was made on 2026-10-20**: the PR still has only the September commits.\n2. Formal AI ne