\n\\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n  link-assistantformal-aiRepository navigationCodeIssues151 (151)Pull requests69 (69)ActionsProjectsSecurity and qualityInsightsMore items\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n      \\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n  Hive Mind 2026-10-20 (0.354.1): Hello World via /claude, /codex and /agent all failed (branch 'so', web_run {} ×210, build outputs left, invalid gh flags, scalac missing, exit code misread, workflow never planned): everything the next release must fix #1364New issueCopy linkNew issueCopy linkOpen#1369OpenHive Mind 2026-10-20 (0.354.1): Hello World via /claude, /codex and /agent all failed (branch 'so', web_run {} ×210, build outputs left, invalid gh flags, scalac missing, exit code misread, workflow never planned): everything the next release must fix#1364#1369Copy linkDescriptionkonardopened on Oct 20, 2026Issue body actionsSummary\\nOn 2026-10-20 Hive Mind 2.39.2 ran the three Hello World issues with Formal AI 0.354.1 as the model, one per client. None succeeded:\\n\\n\\n\\nClient\\nIssue / PR\\nExecution\\nResult\\nWhat Formal AI produced in this run\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nClaude Code (--tool claude)\\nKotlin #1 / PR #2\\n2719fb28\\nfailed, exit 1 after 7 min 28 s\\nSession 1: correct Main.kt, verify script, compiled, ran, committed and pushed 139e03c. Left Main.jar untracked. Session 2 (restart for Main.jar): an invalid gh command, then stopped\\n\\n\\nCodex (--tool codex)\\nRust #1 / PR #2\\nb8b78e59\\nstopped by the operator, exit 137, after 14 h 8 min\\nmain.rs + verify script, compiled and ran, committed. Pushed to branch so (fails), then 210 web_run calls with {} until the sidecar was stopped. No workflow\\n\\n\\nAgent CLI (--tool agent)\\nScala #1 / PR #2\\n2e56df93\\nfailed, exit 1 after 2 h 39 min\\nNothing new: 7 attempts, each repeated the same reads and writes and stopped at scalac: not found\\n\\n\\n\\nGoal of this issue: everything Formal AI must change so that the next release completes all three runs. Each item below has the evidence from these logs, the related issue if one exists, and a regression test built from this exact input. Parts outside Formal AI are listed at the end and tracked in their own repositories.\\nThis continues #1162 (the same three tasks on 2026-09-27 with 0.352.1) and #1328 (the Codex loop of this run, observed live).\\nWhat went wrong, per task\\n1. Claude Code, Kotlin (2719fb28, 14:14 → 14:21 UTC)\\n\\n\\nSession 1 (858bf47a, 7 turns) did the work correctly:\\n\\ngh issue view (title and body);\\nwrote Main.kt and tests/verify-output.sh;\\nran kotlinc Main.kt -include-runtime -d Main.jar, then the verify script (Hello, World!);\\ngit add … &amp;&amp; git commit … &amp;&amp; git push -q origin 'issue-1-604f2202fd18' → 139e03c, pushed.\\n\\nIt ended subtype=success with \\\"Created and verified Main.kt through the agentic CLI harness.\\\"\\n\\n\\nMain.jar was left untracked in the working tree: Formal AI's own build command writes it into the repository root. Hive Mind restarts the session for every uncommitted file (E122: build artifact left untracked, non-idempotent commit chain, and a continuation re-does finished work (Hive Mind restart loop) #1157 has the same symptom from 2026-09-27).\\n\\n\\nSession 2 (539e9b34, 2 turns) got Hive Mind's restart prompt, which lists ?? Main.jar and asks to commit, ignore or delete each file. Formal AI did none of that. Its only step was:\\ngh pr view 'https://github.com/…/pull/2' --comments --json comments,reviews\\n→ Exit code 1: specify only one of --comments or --json\\n\\nIt then ended with \\\"Prepared-work continuation stopped at gh pr view …\\\". The usage error names the fix (--json comments,reviews alone), but Formal AI neither retried it nor moved on to the actual request (Main.jar).\\n\\n\\nHive Mind then stopped with \\\"no progress between sessions\\\" (same HEAD 139e03c, Main.jar still there), exit 1.\\n\\n\\nThe PR content is close to complete: Main.kt, the verify script and .github/workflows/run.yml (from the 2026-09-27 run) are there, and CI passes. What failed the run is the build output and the second session.\\n2. Codex, Rust (b8b78e59, 08:27 → 22:36 UTC)\\nDetails and the live observation are in #1328. Final numbers:\\n\\n08:41:50: rustc main.rs -o main, the verify script passed, and git commit succeeded. git push -q origin 'so' then failed with error: src refspec so does not match any. The branch name came from the system prompt's guideline sentence \\\"commit each atomic step … to the pull request branch so interrupted work remains preserved\\\". The real branch issue-1-09b0c76bd0e4 appears 11 times in the same Codex session (turn_context.git.branch, the prompt).\\n08:43:55 → 16:35:10: 210 codex_apps search_service.web_run calls, all with arguments: {}, all rejected (InvalidActionArgumentsError … missing_required_argument). Before every call the text was the same: \\\"Let me search the web for rust src refspec so does not match any.\\\" There was no repeat stop. Each answer used 57–140 s of a full core, and the request body grew by 864 B per call.\\nAfter the sidecar was stopped (16:35:50), Codex waited \\\"for network\\\" until the operator stopped the task at 22:36. Hive Mind then auto-committed and pushed the untracked main binary (4.5 MB) that Formal AI's rustc main.rs -o main had left in the repository root (693630a). The same build-output problem as Main.jar.\\nRequirement 6 (a GitHub Actions workflow) was never planned: the PR has no workflow and no CI.\\n\\n3. Agent CLI, Scala (2e56df93, 14:28 → 17:07 UTC)\\n\\nEvery attempt repeated the same steps: gh issue view ×2, write Main.scala, write tests/verify-output.sh, scalac Main.scala → /bin/sh: 1: scalac: not found (exit 127), then stop. There were 7 attempts: the first plus 6 Hive Mind retries of the same session; the last one failed at once on the stopped sidecar. scalac ran 8 times. No commit was made on 2026-10-20: the PR still has only the September commits.\\nFormal AI never checked which toolchain exists (command -v scalac, scala-cli, cs, sbt), never tried a fallback, and never handed compilation to CI (the PR already has a workflow that passes). E124: a missing toolchain (scalac: not found) ends the run although rust/src/prerequisite/ and pinned publishers for scalac/kotlinc exist; wire prerequisite recovery into the agentic executor #1159 is the same failure from 2026-09-15.\\nThe tool's exit code was misread. The agent CLI's tool result carries \\\"metadata\\\": {\\\"exit\\\": 127} and \\\"error\\\": \\\"Exit code 127\\\\n/bin/sh: 1: scalac: not found\\\", yet Formal AI answered \\\"Step scalac Main.scala for Main.scala failed. No exit code was reported, so the verdict rests on what the tool said\\\".\\nA resumed session re-ran the steps the history already showed as done (see 0.354.1 loops for 4.5 h at 100% CPU via Codex: pushes to branch 'so' (a word from the prompt), then calls web_run with {} 119 times (wrong 'query' key, no repeat stop) #1328, attempts 1–5).\\n17:07: Hive Mind's retry found the stopped sidecar unreachable and failed the task properly (\\\"the Formal AI endpoint … could not be reached\\\").\\n\\nSidecar, all three runs\\n\\nLogs and memory not written. During the Claude run alone there were 83 level error lines: [dialog-log] failed to record exchange: Permission denied (os error 13), logging_failed_check_log_directory_permissions_and_space. There were also [memory] failed to record live chat exchange: refusing to write an incompatible persisted-memory schema. The permission part is Hive Mind's volume ownership (Formal AI sidecar writes no logs or memory: an existing hive-mind-formal-ai-memory volume stays root-owned (chown only on creation), and its stdout is lost on removal hive-mind#3583). The incompatible persisted-memory schema is Formal AI's: an existing memory volume from an older version can't be used, and nothing upgrades it (compare Support unattended non-destructive persisted-memory upgrades #982).\\nformal-ai serve ignores SIGTERM. docker stop -t 10 ended with exit 137 (0.354.1 loops for 4.5 h at 100% CPU via Codex: pushes to branch 'so' (a word from the prompt), then calls web_run with {} 119 times (wrong 'query' key, no repeat stop) #1328).\\nThe runs used 0.354.1 although v0.355.0 had been released at 2026-10-19 22:37 UTC, about 10 h before the first run. Its notes mention \\\"Preserve observed tool exit status …\\\", \\\"keep explicitly requested workflow paths in fetched coding tasks\\\" and \\\"Continue missing-command recovery …\\\". So items 4, 6 and 7 below may be partly addressed already, but they are unverified for these inputs.\\n\\nWhat Formal AI must fix (each with a regression test from these logs)\\n\\nBranch name from the prompt's prose (so). Push to the checked-out branch (git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD, or the client's git.branch context), never to a word taken from guideline text. Test: the exact Codex system prompt and turn context from b8b78e59 → git push origin issue-1-09b0c76bd0e4. (0.354.1 loops for 4.5 h at 100% CPU via Codex: pushes to branch 'so' (a word from the prompt), then calls web_run with {} 119 times (wrong 'query' key, no repeat stop) #1328)\\nTool calls with empty or invalid arguments, and no repeat stop. web_run must get its input/query. The same failing call with the same arguments must not be planned again: after the second identical failure, change the plan or end the task with an honest failure. Test: the b8b78e59 transcript at item 12 ends in ≤ 2 identical calls. (0.354.1 loops for 4.5 h at 100% CPU via Codex: pushes to branch 'so' (a word from the prompt), then calls web_run with {} 119 times (wrong 'query' key, no repeat stop) #1328)\\nBuild outputs left in the repository (Main.jar, main). Build into a temporary directory, or add a matching .gitignore and commit it, or delete the output after verifying. Never leave an untracked file. Test: Kotlin and Rust tasks end with an empty git status --porcelain. (E122: build artifact left untracked, non-idempotent commit chain, and a continuation re-does finished work (Hive Mind restart loop) #1157)\\nHive Mind's continuation prompt. When the prompt lists uncommitted files, handle each one as asked (commit, ignore or delete) before anything else. A usage error from gh (specify only one of --comments or --json) must be corrected and retried, or skipped, instead of ending the session. Reading PR feedback must use valid flags (gh pr view &lt;n&gt; --json comments,reviews). Test: the 539e9b34 input ends with Main.jar ignored or removed, pushed, and a clean tree. (E123: read PR feedback, update the PR description and mark the PR ready, as a regular LLM does from the same prompt #1158, E122: build artifact left untracked, non-idempotent commit chain, and a continuation re-does finished work (Hive Mind restart loop) #1157)\\nRequirement coverage before success. Check every numbered requirement of the issue before answering success. Here requirement 6 (a GitHub Actions workflow that builds and runs the program on push and pull request) was never planned for Rust, and for Kotlin and Scala it was never checked against the existing run.yml. Test: all three issue bodies → a workflow exists, runs the program and the verify script, and CI is green.\\nMissing toolchain. Probe before compiling (command -v). If the compiler is missing, use an available alternative or install it in user space (e.g. scala-cli / coursier for Scala). As a last resort, commit the source, verify script and workflow and let CI build it, with an honest note that local compilation was not possible. Never stop with the work uncommitted. Test: the Scala issue in an image without scalac → the work is committed and CI is green. (E124: a missing toolchain (scalac: not found) ends the run although rust/src/prerequisite/ and pinned publishers for scalac/kotlinc exist; wire prerequisite recovery into the agentic executor #1159)\\nThe agent CLI's tool-result format. Read state.metadata.exit (and state.error \\\"Exit code N\\\") from OpenCode-style tool_use parts. \\\"No exit code was reported\\\" was false here. Test: the scalac result from 2e56df93. (0.355.0 \\\"Preserve observed tool exit status\\\" may cover this; please confirm with this exact input.)\\nResumed sessions. Continue from the last completed step instead of re-running finished reads, writes and commands. A resume after a completed, committed step should make no further changes. Test: resuming ses_ea64805c8ffe… after attempt 1 does not rewrite Main.scala. (E122: build artifact left untracked, non-idempotent commit chain, and a continuation re-does finished work (Hive Mind restart loop) #1157, 0.354.1 loops for 4.5 h at 100% CPU via Codex: pushes to branch 'so' (a word from the prompt), then calls web_run with {} 119 times (wrong 'query' key, no repeat stop) #1328)\\nEvidence files committed into the user's PR. Both the Kotlin and Rust runs committed dev/log/self-authored/issue-1/evidence/{claude,codex}-stream.jsonl as empty files (0 bytes), plus session-id.txt. Please decide: either commit them with content (and say so in the PR description), or keep them out of the user's repository. An empty evidence file proves nothing and adds noise to a Hello World PR.\\nPersisted-memory schema. Upgrade or migrate an older memory volume unattended and without data loss, or start a new one and say so. Don't refuse every write for the whole session. (Support unattended non-destructive persisted-memory upgrades #982)\\nSIGTERM. formal-ai serve should shut down within the stop timeout instead of being killed (exit 137). (0.354.1 loops for 4.5 h at 100% CPU via Codex: pushes to branch 'so' (a word from the prompt), then calls web_run with {} 119 times (wrong 'query' key, no repeat stop) #1328)\\n\\nOutside Formal AI (tracked in their own repositories)\\n\\nlink-assistant/agent: its own POST /session/&lt;id&gt;/message request is reset after ~256 s (255,992 / 256,052 / 256,215 ms). With Formal AI at 60–140 s per step, every session longer than about 4 minutes hits it.\\nlink-assistant/hive-mind:\\n\\nit takes that reset for a transient network failure and resumes the session (Retry 1–6, 3 → 30 min);\\nits --auto-commit-uncommitted-changes committed and pushed a 4.5 MB compiled binary;\\nthe failed Kotlin run ends with PR Add formal AI proof of concept #2 ready for review, not draft (\\\"Converting PR: To ready for review (run end (No progress between sessions))\\\");\\nthe runs used 0.354.1 although 0.355.0 was out;\\n#3583 (volume ownership).\\n\\n\\nCodex 0.163.0: with a local provider that is down it waits for the network indefinitely instead of failing the turn.\\n\\nAcceptance (the next release)\\n\\n\\nEach fix above has a regression test whose input is taken from these logs (prompts, transcripts, tool results), and the tests run in Formal AI's CI.\\n\\n\\nAgainst a local formal-ai serve --agent-mode, with Claude Code (Kotlin), Codex (Rust) and the Agent CLI (Scala) as clients, using these three issue bodies and these PR branches, each run ends with:\\n\\none program file printing exactly Hello, World! with explaining comments and build/run instructions;\\na verify script and a workflow that runs both on push and pull request, with green CI;\\nno build outputs committed and a clean working tree;\\neverything pushed to the PR branch;\\nthe PR description updated and the PR ready;\\nCLI exit 0.\\n\\nA second run on the same checkout is a no-op success. No run makes more than 2 identical failing tool calls.\\n\\n\\nThen Hive Mind's /claude, /codex and /agent runs of the same three issues all end with ✅ (exit 0) on the released image.\\n\\n\\nLogs (secret gists; the email and Codex account_id are redacted)\\n\\nClaude Code / Kotlin, execution 2719fb28, 14:14 → 14:21 UTC: https://gist.github.com/konard/bde1161e75014632ee711c07328f21b9\\nCodex / Rust, execution b8b78e59, 08:27 → 22:36 UTC: https://gist.github.com/konard/fc014070fb8976cd3ad7766ed0675c0a\\nAgent CLI / Scala, execution 2e56df93, 14:28 → 17:07 UTC: https://gist.github.com/konard/74beb03d2d22bfaf8bb8b96dc6bd73e1\\nFormal AI 0.354.1 sidecar stdout, 08:27 → 16:35 UTC: https://gist.github.com/konard/64cec5f80bec8275df4d255399a7e80e\\nCodex rollout 01a1586d (to 15:31 UTC) and earlier logs: in 0.354.1 loops for 4.5 h at 100% CPU via Codex: pushes to branch 'so' (a word from the prompt), then calls web_run with {} 119 times (wrong 'query' key, no repeat stop) #1328\\nReactions are currently unavailableActivitykonardadded a parent issue on Oct 20, 2026E118: Hive Mind 2026-09-27 (0.352.1): deliver the Hello World PR like a regular LLM does; codex read loop, agent gh fallback, doubled output, idempotent commit, PR feedback/description/ready (sub-issues) #1162Sign up for free to join this conversation on GitHub. Already have an account? Sign in to commentMetadataMetadataAssigneesNo one assignedLabelsNo labelsNo labelsTypeNo typeProjectsNo projectsMilestoneNo milestoneRelationshipsNone yetDevelopmentNo branches or pull requestsIssue actionsOpen in GitHub Copilot app\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n\\n    \\n  \\n\\n  \\n\\n          \\n  Footer\\n\\n  \\n\\n\\n  \\n    \\n      \\n        \\n    \\n\\n\\n      \\n        &copy; 2026 GitHub,&nbsp;Inc.\\n      \\n    \\n\\n    \\n      Footer navigation\\n\\n      \\n\\n\\n          \\n            Terms\\n          \\n\